---
import Summary from '../components/Summary.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Divider from '../components/Divider.astro';
---
<Base title={"Depression Therapy in Utah & Provo | Tangible Therapy"} description={"Depression therapy in Utah — evidence-based support to lift the weight, restore energy & feel like yourself again. Insurance accepted, avg $25/session. Free consult."}>
<section class="sec t-black h-medium has-bg has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-bg"><img src="/images/tangible-33-b74a9f.jpg" alt="" style="object-position:51% 18%" loading="eager"><div class="sec-ov" style="opacity:0.5"></div></div><div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:7;--mrows:10">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/5/6/23;--m:1/2/7/10"><div class="rte"><h1 class="ta-center">Depression Therapy</h1><p class="lg ta-center">Therapy that helps you feel like yourself again</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-button jc" style="--d:6/11/8/18;--m:7/2/9/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><div class="btn-wrap ta-center"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-medium btn-full" href="https://tangible.clientsecure.me/">Start Depression Counseling Today</a></div></div>
</div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#fff" /></section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:12;--mrows:22">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/16/12/26;--m:14/2/22/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:40px"><img src="/images/adobestock-570145624-ea0d38.jpeg" alt="A woman in a light blue blouse sits on a sofa, hand on chest, speaking intently to a black male therapist facing her. The setting is calm and professional." width="7546" height="5033" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:3/2/5/12;--m:2/2/4/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>When everything feels heavy</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:5/2/10/12;--m:4/2/15/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>Depression doesn’t always look like sadness. Sometimes it’s numbness. Exhaustion. Going through the motions while everything feels dull or meaningless. Getting out of bed, answering messages, or doing basic tasks can feel impossible.</p><p>If you’re tired of pretending you’re fine — or feeling like you’ll never feel like yourself again — depression therapy can help.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-black h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:12;--mrows:20">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/2/12/12;--m:13/2/20/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:40px;--fp:50% 66%"><img src="/images/depression-108e01.jpg" alt="Two women sit across from eachother in a warmly lit room filled with plants. The female therapist is leaning back while guiding the client through counseling for depression." width="3300" height="2550" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:3/15/5/25;--m:2/2/5/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>Depression isn’t a weakness</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:5/15/10/25;--m:5/2/13/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>Depression is a real, treatable condition, not a personal failure. It can be triggered by grief, trauma, burnout, or nothing obvious at all. No matter how it started, it’s not your fault; you don’t have to stay stuck.</p><p>Our therapists are here to listen, guide, and support you through it without judgment or pressure.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:15;--mrows:23">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/5/13;--m:2/2/5/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>What depression therapy helps with</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/16/14/26;--m:16/2/23/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:40px"><img src="/images/tangible-47-9c7b1b.jpg" alt="A group therapy setting filled with plants and brightly lit. The group sits in a circle talking." width="3300" height="2550" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:5/2/14/13;--m:5/2/16/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>We work with people experiencing:</p><ul><li><p>Persistent sadness or hopelessness</p></li><li><p>Fatigue, low motivation, or brain fog</p></li><li><p>Irritability or emotional numbness</p></li><li><p>Isolation or disconnection from others</p></li><li><p>Negative self-talk and low self-worth</p></li><li><p>Loss of interest in things that once mattered</p></li></ul><p>Whether your depression is mild, moderate, or severe, therapy offers a way forward — at your pace, in your words.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-black h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:12;--mrows:23">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:1/2/12/12;--m:12/2/19/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:40px"><img src="/images/tangible-30-3272eb.jpg" alt="A black female therapist conducts therapy virtually over telehealth with a young woman who has a red shirt and is smiling" width="2500" height="1603" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/15/4/25;--m:2/2/4/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>You're allowed to feel better</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:4/15/8/25;--m:4/2/11/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>Depression convinces you that nothing will help. But we’ve seen people step out of the dark, reconnect with themselves, and reclaim their lives. You don’t have to stay stuck in survival mode.</p><p>When you’re ready, we’re here.</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-button jc" style="--d:9/15/11/22;--m:20/2/22/10;--dz:5;--mz:5"><div class="btn-wrap ta-center"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-medium btn-full" href="https://tangible.clientsecure.me/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Schedule Your First Session</a></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-in" style="padding-top:6.6vmax;padding-bottom:6.6vmax">
<div class="wrap"><div class="list-title rte"><p>What you’ll get</p></div><ul class="ulist ulist-carousel" style="--per:3;--ar:3/2;--tfs:calc((2.2 - 1) * var(--fs-unit) + 1rem);--bfs:calc((1.2 - 1) * var(--fs-unit) + 1rem);--cw:75%;--gap:20px"><li class="li"><a class="li-link" href="#" aria-label="✺"></a><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Recognize thought patterns that fuel depression</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Rebuild motivation in small, manageable steps</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Practice self-compassion and emotional regulation</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Improve sleep, energy, and daily functioning</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Reconnect with parts of yourself you’ve been missing</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><a class="li-link" href="/" aria-label="✺"></a><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Set boundaries to protect yourself</p></div></div></li></ul><div class="carousel-nav"><button class="prev" aria-label="Previous"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M19 12H5m6-6-6 6 6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></button><button class="next" aria-label="Next"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></button></div></div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#565d57" /></section>

<section class="sec t-light h-medium">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:16;--mrows:7">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/7/3/22;--m:1/2/3/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">Depression Therapists</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-summary-v2" style="--d:3/5/17/24;--m:3/2/8/10"><Summary kind="team" design="carousel" category="telehealth/depression" limit={9} perRow={3} rounded /></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-black h-medium">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:13;--mrows:20">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/4/26;--m:1/2/4/10"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">✺ Frequently asked questions ✺</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/2/14/13;--m:5/2/13/10"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>Do I need a diagnosis to start therapy?</summary><div class="rte"><p>No. You're welcome here whether you’ve been formally diagnosed or are simply feeling off. We’ll help you explore what you’re experiencing and what support makes sense for you.</p></div></details><details><summary>What kind of therapy do you use for depression?</summary><div class="rte"><p>We use a range of evidence-based approaches like CBT, Internal Family Systems, EMDR, and somatic tools. Your therapist will choose what’s most helpful based on your needs and preferences.</p></div></details><details><summary>What if I don’t feel like talking much?</summary><div class="rte"><p>That’s okay. Depression can make talking hard. We’ll move slowly, with no pressure. You’ll have space to process things in your own way, whether that’s through conversation, reflection, or skill-building.</p></div></details></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/15/10/26;--m:13/2/21/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>Can therapy help even if I’ve felt this way for years?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Yes. Change is possible even if you’ve been feeling low for a long time. We’ll start where you are and work together to shift what’s been keeping you stuck.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you work with clients who are also taking medication?`</summary><div class="rte"><p>Yes. Therapy works well alongside medication, and we support whatever combination gives you the most relief. If needed, we’re happy to coordinate care with your prescriber.</p></div></details></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</Base>
